 "circuits": [],
 "equations": [],
 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "The range",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "All nine share the 2.0 A average current, 50 A surge, storage temperature and thermal ratings. VRRM steps from 20 V to 200 V. VF max at 2 A is 0.55 V for SS22B to SS24B, 0.70 V for SS25B and SS26B, 0.85 V for SS28B to SS215B and 0.95 V for SS220B. IR max at 25 °C is 1.0 mA for SS22B to SS210B and 0.2 mA for SS215B and SS220B. CJ typ is 220 pF for SS22B to SS24B and 180 pF for SS25B to SS220B. Tj max is 125 °C for SS22B to SS26B and 150 °C for SS28B to SS220B."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Temperature derating",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Average current stays at 2 A up to a lead temperature of about 113 °C for SS22B to SS26B and about 97 °C for SS28B to SS220B, then falls in a straight line to zero at about 150 °C and 125 °C respectively."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Surge",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The 50 A peak is for one 8.3 ms half sine; with repeated cycles the allowed peak drops, to about 25 A at 10 cycles and about 13 A at 100."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Leakage",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "On the typical curves reverse current climbs slowly with the share of rated peak reverse voltage applied: at Tj = 100 °C from about 1.4 to 4.7 mA for SS22B to SS26B and 0.24 to 0.94 mA for SS28B to SS220B; at Tj = 25 °C from about 0.004 to 0.022 mA and 0.001 to 0.004 mA."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Mechanical",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The case is DO-214AA (SMB). Mould compound is rated UL 94V-0, RoHS-compliant and halogen-free. Terminals are solder plated and solderable to MIL-STD-750 method 2026. Moisture sensitivity is MSL 1 per J-STD-020, with a 260 °C lead-free peak. A band on the body marks the cathode end. Unit weight is 0.098 g."
  }
 ],
